{"connection_phase":"streaming","connection_type":"https/sse","model":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"Claude","session_id":"session_gorilla_1792419868844_52703e0bec7a07cb","status_detail":null,"text":"The ledger task is finished. `bun test` passes (3/3), and I checked the CLI by hand against `data/sample.csv` and some edge cases.\n\n- **`src/csv.ts`**: The CSV reader now follows the format in TASK.md. It handles quoted fields with commas, line breaks and `\"\"` inside them, both line ending styles, and a trailing newline. Empty lines are dropped.\n- **`src/money.ts`**: `parseAmount` checks each amount against the regex in TASK.md and works out cents from the digits directly, so no rounding goes through floats. It throws on every invalid example in the spec (empty, `abc`, `1.234`, `1.2.3`, `12,34`, `+5`, `.5`). `formatCents` always shows 2 decimals with a `-` for negatives, like `-0.05`.\n- **`src/report.ts`**: Category names are trimmed. Rows with the wrong number of columns or a bad amount are skipped and counted, and blank lines are ignored without counting.\n- **`src/cli.ts`** (new): It prints categories sorted by total (largest first, ties by name) and then the `TOTAL` line, and writes `skipped: N` to stderr when rows were skipped. It exits with 1 when the file can't be read and 2 when no file is given.\n\nThings I added that the spec doesn't mention:\n- `-0` is accepted and returns 0.\n- Lines containing only spaces count as blank, so they aren't counted as skipped.\n- The CLI strips a byte-order mark at the start of the file, which some spreadsheet exports add.\n\nEverything is committed in one commit (0995bbb).","type":"done","upstream_provider":null,"usage":{"cache_creation_input_tokens":395,"cache_read_input_tokens":31352,"input_tokens":110,"output_tokens":586}}
